  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ENTRYPOINT is the executable; CMD supplies default arguments (or the whole command if there's no ENTRYPOINT). Run-time args replace CMD; `--entrypoint` replaces ENTRYPOINT."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "ENTRYPOINT",
        "CMD",
        "`docker run img`",
        "`docker run img migrate`"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "—",
          "[\"uvicorn\",\"app:app\"]",
          "uvicorn app:app",
          "migrate"
        ],
        [
          "[\"python\",\"-m\",\"app\"]",
          "[\"serve\"]",
          "python -m app serve",
          "python -m app migrate"
        ],
        [
          "[\"/entrypoint.sh\"]",
          "[\"uvicorn\",\"app:app\"]",
          "/entrypoint.sh uvicorn app:app",
          "/entrypoint.sh migrate"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "",
        "Exec form `[\"bin\",\"arg\"]`",
        "Shell form `bin arg`"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "PID 1",
          "Your binary",
          "/bin/sh -c"
        ],
        [
          "Signals",
          "Reach the app",
          "Swallowed by sh"
        ],
        [
          "$VAR expansion",
          "No",
          "Yes"
        ],
        [
          "Needs a shell",
          "No",
          "Yes"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Expansion with correct signals",
      "level": 2,
      "numbered": false
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "code": "ENTRYPOINT [\"/entrypoint.sh\"]\nCMD [\"uvicorn\", \"app.main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8000\"]",
      "language": "dockerfile"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "code": "#!/bin/sh\nset -e\n: \"${PORT:=8000}\"\nexec \"$@\"",
      "language": "sh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Single variable: `CMD [\"sh\",\"-c\",\"exec uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8000}\"]`."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "variant": "warning",
      "text": "Exec form must be valid JSON. `CMD ['uvicorn','app:app']` (single quotes) silently falls back to shell form. Setting ENTRYPOINT also resets any inherited CMD, so redeclare it."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "variant": "important",
      "text": "Q: \"CMD vs ENTRYPOINT, and why exec form?\" A: \"ENTRYPOINT is the fixed executable, CMD the overridable default args. Exec form runs the binary directly as PID 1 so it receives SIGTERM; shell form wraps it in sh, which swallows signals.\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Key takeaways",
      "level": 2,
      "numbered": false
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Run args replace CMD, not ENTRYPOINT.",
        "Exec form = signals work.",
        "Need expansion? Wrapper script plus exec.",
        "Double quotes only in exec form."
      ]
    }
  ]
}